* kisi 0.3.3: lane BUS_P as a SPICE subcircuit (ngspice, Xyce, LTspice, KiCad)
* board board.kicad_pcb
* subcircuit BUS_P_lane (pair: P and N on their own paths, coupled sections in modal form)
* port 1 (ap): P BUS_P at U1.6 (transmitter end)
* port 2 (an): N BUS_N at U1.7 (transmitter end)
* port 3 (bp): P BUS_P at U2.6 (receiver end)
* port 4 (bn): N BUS_N at U2.7 (receiver end)
* track length 55.75 mm, delay 315.3 ps, reference 50.00 ohm per port
* model (compact): kisi's channel sections; lines as lossless-line cells (at least 3 per delay x 10.00 GHz): per cell
*   a lossless LC ladder (40 sections per wavelength: the delay) and the fitted Foster (R(f), L_int(f)) and Debye
*   (G(f), C(f)) networks lumped once; consecutive sections with the same model merged (5 merges); vias as kisi's
*   via ladder, parts with estimated parasitics, open stubs; coupled sections of a pair as even/odd chains between
*   ideal mode converters (E/F). Passive and causal by construction.
* check against kisi's S-parameters (same model): |dS21| <= 0.09985 dB to 1.5 x Nyquist (3.411 dB to the top), largest |dS| 0.01595 to 1.5 x Nyquist (0.4511 to the top)
* fits of the main line sections (each at least 10 % of the length): R 0.5976 %, X 0.04508 %, G 95.98 %, B 13.31 %; via ladders 0 %
* elements after flattening: 714 R, 771 L, 627 C, 80 sources; 0 RLGC sections, 56 lossless-line cells
* usage: X1 ap an bp bn 0 BUS_P_lane   (the last port is the reference)
* stackup: 2 copper layers, 1.49 mm, er and tand at 1 GHz; from board file (layer by layer in the README)
*   layers (um): F.Cu 30 / 1430 er 4.42 tand 0.02 / B.Cu 30

